nerator's f_back is None (its caller may be reused: releaseFrame)"] [98 5 "// callInit's __init__ returned: the instance is the call's value (type_call's check of __init__'s)"] [111 4 "// a call of a Python function from f: run the callee in this loop"] [126 5 "// the callee's RESUME: the eval breaker (PY6f's thread_gil.go), its error raised in the callee; then"] [127 5 "// sys.monitoring's PY_START (queue 220: breakMonitor keeps the breaker set while a tool has events)"] [138 3 "// an exception in f at f.Lasti"] [144 4 "// an exception the runtime raised in f (a KeyError of d[k] ...): chained as _PyErr_SetObject chains"] [149 23 "// a re-raise adds no entry for the frame it is raised in (exception_unwind)"] [153 38 "// RAISE (queue 219t): settrace's 'exception'"] [162 47 "// frame->instr_ptr: a reraise N's restored instruction"] [168 24 "// PY_UNWIND (queue 220)"] [181 1 "// OpImpl implements an operation outside step's switch (PYI-SPEC.md §7.5): it pops and pushes f's"] [182 1 "// stack itself and returns (nil, nil) to go on; (nil, err) raises; (nil, *pushFrame) runs a Python"] [183 1 "// function's frame next; (v, nil) makes f return v (a generator's yield sets f.Suspended first)."] [186 1 "// opImpls are the operations registered by the files that own them (§9), each by its file's init:"] [187 1 "// RegisterOp(OpLoadAttr, ...). An operation of step's switch is never looked up here."] [190 1 "// RegisterOp sets op's implementation; a second one is a programming error (one owner per operation)."] [198 1 "// pushFrame is step's signal that the instruction called a Python function: not an exception."] [201 1 "// callStack is call [N KWNAMES]: the callable under its N arguments on f's stack (the last len(kwnames) of them"] [202 1 "// keywords), all popped; a Python function's frame (a bound method's, its self first) made from the arguments"] [203 1 "// where they are on the stack and returned as the thread's *pushFrame, a generator made, or any other callable"] [204 1 "// called and its value pushed (202b: the arguments were copied off the stack, then again with self in front)."] [206 22 "// sys.monitoring's CALL, C_RETURN, C_RAISE (queue 220)"] [218 24 "// the callable's slot holds self: the arguments are self's and the stack's"] [230 4 "// a built-in method bound to its object (BuiltinType's call slot): its arguments made at once with self"] [231 4 "// first (queue 210: they were copied off the stack, then again behind self)"] [260 3 "// CPython's RETURN_GENERATOR: the frame kept in its generator, coroutine or async generator"] [267 1 "// directMax bounds the direct calls (callDirect) nested on the thread's Go stack at once: each holds its caller's Go"] [268 1 "// frames while its callee runs, so a deeper chain (a recursion past it, up to any recursion limit) goes on as pushed"] [269 1 "// frames, in the innermost loop, with no Go frames per Python call (queue 216d)."] [272 1 "// enter is a call's callee frame (made, its arguments bound) run from f: when f and the callee are both compiled,"] [273 1 "// directly by f's own Go code (callDirect: its value pushed on f's stack, or its exception returned); else returned"] [274 1 "// as the thread's *pushFrame, read by runFrames before the thread's next call."] [283 1 "// callDirect runs callee, a compiled function's frame called by f's compiled code (queue 216d, the user's (a) on"] [284 1 "// 216's DECISION 1): a loop of its own (runFrames, direct) with callee its entry frame, entered as runFrames enters a"] [285 1 "// pushed frame (f_back f, the recursion limit's check raising in f, the eval breaker's error in callee, no C level),"] [286 1 "// so its exception unwinds through callee's handlers and leaves it with callee's traceback entry, then f's code"] [287 1 "// returns it and f's loop adds f's; its value pushed on f's stack, or callInit's instance (an __init__ returning"] [288 1 "// anything but None the TypeError raised in f), as runFrames pushes a returning pushed frame's."] 